## Upstream Projects

This project would not exist without these excellent open-source projects:

| Project | Author/Organization | License | Purpose |
|---------|---------------------|---------|---------|
| **LuxTTS** | Yatharth Sharma (@ysharma3501) | MIT (likely) | Voice cloning text-to-speech |
| **Whisper MLX** | Apple Inc. / MLX team | MIT | Apple Silicon speech-to-text |
| **FastAPI** | Sebastián Ramírez (@tiangolo) | MIT | Web framework |
| **Linacodec** | Yatharth Sharma (@ysharma3501) | Unknown (likely MIT) | Vocoder for LuxTTS |
| **PyTorch** | PyTorch Team / Meta | BSD-style | Deep learning framework |
| **transformers** | Hugging Face | Apache 2.0 | Model loading |
| **lhotse** | Lhotse team | Apache 2.0 | Audio data handling |
| **MLX** | Apple Inc. | MIT | Apple machine learning |

## Special Thanks

- **OpenAI** — For the OpenAI-compatible API specification that enables interoperability
- **Home Assistant Wyoming Protocol** — For the streaming voice architecture inspiration
- **FastAPI community** — For excellent documentation and examples

---

This project represents an integration effort — combining multiple specialized tools 
into a cohesive, OpenAI-compatible server optimized for Apple Silicon. All credit 
for the underlying TTS/STT engines belongs to their respective authors.
